    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0202" n="102" xml:id="pg102"/>

                <head>No. 88.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Torreão de
                    Barros.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 30,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It is with much pleasure that I inform you
                    hereby, with reference to your recent announcement of the intention of the
                    Emperor to send an embassy to China to enter into certain treaties of amity and
                    commerce with the government of that country, that the President sincerely
                    sympathizes with the desire of the Emperor to extend and confirm his friendly
                    relations with that government, and will give orders that the representative of
                    the United States in China shall extend to the Brazilian representative in that
                    country the friendly welcome and the moral support which is naturally to be
                    expected from the intimate relations so happily existing between the United
                    States and Brazil.</p>
                <p>I profit by this occasion, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">B. E. Torreão de Barros</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
